{
  "_about": "Battle camera director shots (Technical Artist), from Ross's storyboard docs/storyboards/battle_camera_ross_2026-10-07.jpg. A shot is keyframes of camera position, look-at target, roll (degrees) and FOV (degrees), eased over a duration. Positions and targets are an anchor (mid, party, enemy, hero0..2, foe0..3, boss, actor, target, pair_mid) plus an offset [along the foes-to-heroes axis, up, toward the camera side]; offsets are scaled by the formation's size, so shots fit any party or enemy layout. frame 'pair' uses the axis through the acting pair (target toward actor). Times are milliseconds. The camera pose updates at director.pose_hz (stepped, PSX chunky).",
